{"timestamp":"2026-08-13T23:12:18Z","action":"complaint","word":"t","murky":" the cursor comes from a `:hover` rule — [File_Content.svelte:947](ov/src/lib/svelte/content/File_Content.svelte#L947).\n\nThey are made in the file's own words rather than written in the markup, so the action cannot be put on them the way every other control got it; the target would have to be made and thrown away alongside each mark, and the whole run of them is rebuilt whenever a fold changes.","plain":"No, they are not wired.\n\nEvery other control is written in the markup, so the action can be put on it. A soft pointer is not: the app builds it in code and pushes it into the drawn page, then throws every one away and builds them again each time a fold changes.\n\nSo wiring them means making and unmaking a target alongside each mark by hand."}
